body:
The left side can be a real boolean (`param.isBool()` is true) or a truthy/falsy value. `asBool()` only checks for a truthy/falsy value.

When the left side is a real boolean, replace it with a boolean literal. Similar to the two cases above.

When the left side is a truthy/falsy value AND the right side is not dropped, also replace it with a boolean literal.

When the left side is a truthy/falsy value BUT the right side is not dropped, keep the left side and visit it with `parser.walkExpression(expression.left)` instead.

This will handle cases like:

``` js
const value1 = "hello" || expr();
const value2 = DEFINED_AS_TRUE || expr();
const value3 = "" && expr();
const value4 = DEFINED_AS_FALSE && expr();
const value5 = "hello" && expr();
const value6 = "" || expr();
expect(value1).toBe("hello");
expect(value2).toBe(true);
expect(value3).toBe("");
expect(value4).toBe(false);
expect(value5).toBe(expr());
expect(value6).toBe(expr());
```

Generated code:

``` js
const value1 = "hello" || false;
const value2 = true || false;
const value3 = "" && false;
const value4 = false && false;
const value5 = true && expr();
const value6 = false || expr();
expect(value1).toBe("hello");
expect(value2).toBe(true);
expect(value3).toBe("");
expect(value4).toBe(false);
expect(value5).toBe(expr());
expect(value6).toBe(expr());
```

Add test cases for this. This can't be statsCases, but should be `test/cases` instead.

For `DEFINED_AS_TRUE` you can use `typeof require === "function"` and for `DEFINED_AS_FALSE` `typeof require !== "function"`. These evaluate to `true` and `false`

